          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "# This program uses variables to store and display information.\n# Variables are like containers that hold data.\n\n# Here, we create a variable named 'message' and put text inside it.\nmessage = \"Hello, future programmer!\"\nprint(message)\n\n# You can change the value stored in a variable:\nmessage = \"Now the message is different.\"\nprint(message)\n\nprint(\"---------------------------------\")\nprint(\"Your turn!\")\n\n# TODO 1: Create a variable called 'my_name' and assign your name (as text in quotes) to it.\n# Example: my_name = \"Ada\"\n\n\n# TODO 2: Now, use a print() statement to display a greeting using your 'my_name' variable.\n# For example: print(\"Nice to meet you, \" + my_name)\n\n\n# TODO 3: Create another variable called 'my_age' and assign your age (as a number, without quotes) to it.\n# Example: my_age = 10\n\n\n# TODO 4: Add another print() statement to display your age.\n# For example: print(\"You are \" + str(my_age) + \" years old.\")\n# (Hint: You might need to convert the number to text using str() if combining with other text.)\n",
          "folderId": "0",
